  "headline": "Queen of the Arabian Sea",
  "short_description": "Kochi's Fort Kochi district layers Portuguese, Dutch and British colonial history over an ancient spice-trading port.",
  "about": "A historic port city where Chinese fishing nets, Jewish synagogues, Portuguese churches and Kerala backwaters converge in Fort Kochi and Mattancherry.\n\nLocated on the Malabar Coast of Kerala, spread across islands and a mainland connected by bridges and ferries.\n\nHome to Kathakali and Kalaripayattu performance traditions, and a fusion of Kerala, European and Jewish heritage.\n\nDiverse Hindu, Christian, Muslim and historically Jewish communities.",
  "history": "A major hub of the spice trade for over 600 years, successively controlled by Kerala rulers, the Portuguese, the Dutch and the British.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Cochin International Airport (airport)\n- Ernakulam Junction (railway)\n- Kochi KSRTC Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Malayalam, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2 days",
